			<div class="content" id="post-content-1479119">
									

<p>Nay good sir. Especially since chaps were specifically designed to be worn over jeans (something folks playing dress-up intentionally forget) to protect the clothing and legs from either dense terrain such as thickets, or incidental contact while herding cattle. It's believed that they originated from copying similar styles from Native American tribes.</p>
<p>Fun fact: this is also why bikers wear leather and denim, because they're a combination of comfortable clothes that will keep your skin from looking like hamburger if you wipe out. Unless you're one of those fine fellows that wears an open leather vest and no shirt or helmet.</p>

